      "title": "Assistant Professor of Data Analytics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nAssistant Professor of Data Analytics Ohio Wesleyan University’s  Data Analytics program  invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Data Analytics to begin in August 2027. We seek an enthusiastic colleague and instructor with deep professional experience in a range of disciplinary Data Analytics applications. We encourage applicants from any academic field (e.g., social sciences, humanities, or natural sciences) that possess strong data analytics expertise and experience to apply. OWU’s Data Analytics program is an interdisciplinary program grounded in the liberal arts. In addition to courses in Data Analytics, Mathematics, and Computer Science, students also study in several cognate disciplines, including Politics and Government, Psychology, Physics, Geography, Finance, Environmental Studies, Economics,  Anthropology and Sociology,  and Accounting. Throughout, students consider the ethical implications of their work and develop problem-solving skills that draw upon habits and methods of a range of disciplines. The successful candidate will join a faculty and interdisciplinary community with a wide range of research and teaching interests and will benefit from extensive support for junior faculty, including start-up funding, pre-tenure research leave, funding for student-faculty research collaboration via the  Summer Scholarship & Research Program  and  The OWU Connection , and a range of workshops and mentoring programs supported by the endowed  Smith Center for Faculty Excellence .  This job is part of a cluster of positions focused on flexibility, interdisciplinarity, and inclusivity. The faculty cohort will join an educational community that values interdisciplinarity and fosters close working relationships with students through our signature program in experiential learning, the OWU Connection. Incoming faculty will be provided with mentoring, professional development, funds, and opportunities to connect with faculty across the  Ohio 5  and  GLCA consortia . For more information about the cluster, please visit  www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty . . Responsibilities Collaborate in teaching six program or department courses a year (3/3), including several existing DATA courses such as Introduction to Data Analytics, Social, Ethical, and Cultural Impacts of Big Data, Data Visualization and Presentation, Methods in Data Analytics, and Capstone. Assist in developing and expanding OWU’s Data Analytics program, including the creation of new classes in Data Analytics or in a cognate discipline. Advise and mentor students in their academic journey. Engage in a consistent and focused line of research. Provide service to the program, university, and profession. Assist in curriculum development, revision, and evaluation. Qualifications Ph.D. or Master’s degree in analytics, data science, or a related field Evidence of preparation for teaching at the undergraduate level. Interest in or experience with mentoring undergraduates, including students entering data analytics from a range of academic backgrounds and levels of preparation. A research agenda in data analytics or a related field. Application Materials Applicants should submit the following: Cover Letter CV Teaching and Student Engagement Statement (2-page limit): Please provide a statement that articulates your teaching philosophy. In your response, address your ability to teach a broad range of courses and to employ pedagogical approaches that support students with varied perspectives and experiences. Describe how you connect students with opportunities, resources, and networks that expand their access to your field of study. Include examples of outreach, advising, or program activities that have supported students whose pathways into the discipline may not follow a traditional trajectory. Research statement (2-page limit): A statement outlining the central aims of the research program you would like to develop, how it will thrive at Ohio Wesleyan, and how you will involve OWU students in your research. Please submit all materials via  www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty , where you will find additional information about working at OWU. Official transcripts, reference letters, and additional materials may be requested at a later time, and can be sent directly to  facultyjobs@owu.edu . Please make sure to include “Data Analytics” in the subject line. Questions may be directed to Mehwish Abbasi, search chair  (mabbasi@owu.edu) . Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. About Ohio Wesleyan Located in the Columbus, Ohio metropolitan area, Ohio Wesleyan is a selective   residential liberal arts college enrolling approximately 1,600+ students from across the nation and around the world. The college’s signature program,  the OWU Connection , empowers students to complete research, community service, careers, and study abroad, teaching students to apply their knowledge in real-world settings. Ohio Wesleyan is featured in the book  Colleges That Change Lives  and was recently listed as the No. 1 liberal arts college in Ohio for social mobility by  U.S. News and World Report . OWU is located in Delaware, OH, a lively college town just 30 minutes from Columbus, the 14th most populous city in the United States and part of the fastest growing, most economically vibrant areas of the Midwest. Columbus, known increasingly as the “Silicon Midwest,” was named by LinkedIn as one of the top 10 U.S. cities in which to launch your career.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201845493393_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Athletics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nAthletics-SW The OWU Athletics Department is looking to hire Student Workers Athletics Game Management  SQ Fitness Center  Morrill Fitness Center    Summary: The Athletics Department is seeking enthusiastic and reliable student workers to assist in supporting the daily operations, events, and activities within the department. This position provides students with the opportunity to gain valuable experience in a fast-paced and dynamic environment while contributing to the success of our athletic programs.   Tasks & Responsibilities:  Game Management:  This position will assist with various gameday operational positions at home athletic events. Positions include game presentation roles (music, video board, scoreboard, PA, etc.), implementing in-game promotions, sideline ball helpers, setup and teardown of events, as well as other duties as needed.    SQ/Morrill Fitness Center: This position serves as the primary customer service representative for the Simpson-Querrey Fitness Center and/or Morrill Strength & Conditioning Room and is responsible for:  Greeting and welcoming members/guests with a smile and friendly attitude. Upholding, enforcing and clearly communicating rules and regulations of fitness center.  Performing duties at desks; including, but not limited to checking IDs to ensure proper patron access to facility, rental of recreational equipment, and maintaining user counts.  Monitoring, organizing and cleaning the fitness center (including workspace); maintaining a presentable environment for users.  Performing laundry of towels, as well as re-filling equipment cleaning bottles.  Attending any required meetings or training sessions.  Regular attendance of assigned shifts.  Additional Responsibilities: Event Support: Assist with game-day operations, including setup and teardown of equipment, ticketing, concessions, and crowd management. Customer Service: Greet and assist guests, athletes, and staff, providing information and addressing inquiries professionally.  Help maintain athletic facilities, ensuring cleanliness, organization, and readiness for practices, games, and events. Equipment Management: Organize and distribute athletic gear, maintain inventory, and assist in equipment upkeep. Marketing and Promotions: Support the promotion of athletic events through social media, flyer distribution, and event signage. Other Duties: Complete additional tasks as assigned by supervisors to support the department’s operations.  Any previous experience working athletic events is preferred, but not required.  Must be dependable, and be able to work nights and weekends. Comfortable standing, walking, and performing physical tasks for extended periods. Other tasks as assigned. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States Application Instructions:  Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Abby Stoner Commitment: 15-20 hours per week Term: Fall 26 & Spring 27, part-time position",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200985587928_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Worker - ECC Crossing Guard",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker – ECC Crossing Guard Purpose/Objective of the Role: The Service Learning office and the Early Childhood Center (ECC) are partnering to make Park Ave safer for our preschool program! We are hiring students each semester to serve as Crossing Guards at the ECC Monday thru Friday during the Early Childhood Center's arrival and dismissal times. A portion of the shift will be outdoors, so appropriately dressing for the weather is a must! Tasks & Responsibilities: Applicants must commit to the full semester Complete the provided training  Attend every assigned shift  Assist ECC families by ensuring a safe crosswalk during arrival and departure times Communication with the ECC Director and Teachers/Staff Assist with small ECC projects, as time allows Qualifications: Excellent communication skills Time management skills Unwavering commitment to attendance Passion for working with children and fostering a positive environment Federal Work Study Recipient (preferred, not required) Potential Future Career Benefit:  The ECC Crossing Guard program provides a fulfilling experience for students interested in any field that requires interacting with the public by enhancing communication and interpersonal skills. This position will allow interactions with the ECC staff, enrolled students and their families. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Kerri Robe Commitment: 1-3 hours per week Term: temporary, part-time position  (Fall-26 & Spring-27)",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200982674066_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Electrician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-28\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nOhio Wesleyan University ( www.owu.edu ), a selective, private, undergraduate liberal arts, residential institution founded in 1842 and is located just 20 miles north of Columbus, is seeking dynamic,  skilled candidates for the position of Electrician . This is a fulltime, hourly position.    RESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE – BUT NOT LIMITED TO :   This individual reports directly to the Electrical Trades Supervisor and is responsible to install, test, and service the electrical light and power distribution circuits, equipment, appliances, fire alarms systems, and other related electrical services at the University.    This position will also be responsible for the testing and maintaining of life safety systems including but not limited to fire alarm systems and devices,  egress lighting, fire extinguishers, elevator emergency phones and other tasks that are code required. This person will be required to keep accurate records.     QUALIFICATIONS /SKILLS:   A high school diploma or equivalent is required.   Also, required is seven years previous experience with commercial/industrial electric or have completed a four-year apprenticeship.   The electrician must also have a valid Ohio Driver’s License.  Must be capable of independent judgment and be able to be guided by oral or written instructions to complete the associated tasks/responsibilities.     Must be able to work from blueprints or sketches. Must have knowledge of electrical codes and standards written by the National Electrical Code, National Fire Protection Agency (particularly Articles 70 & 72), OSHA requirements,  and the  safe practices associated with this trade. Must be able to lift and handle weights common to this trade and work at heights up to 35 feet from either a scaffold or a ladder. Be on emergency call-in rotation schedule.   FACTORS CONTRIBUTING TO SUCCESS: Thorough knowledge of methods, tools, and practices used in the electrical trade Thorough knowledge of the hazards and safety precautions particular to the trade Good communication skills and ability to work effectively with other people Near visual acuity, skill in interpreting technical literature, blueprints, drawings and manufacturer’s instructions Knowledge of Life Safety systems, fire alarms, emergency backup systems and applicable codes WORKING CONDITIONS:  May perform work in all University facilities and is subject to possible exposure to chemicals, gases, electrical shock; may work in confined spaces on ladders.         NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States.   What We Offer:   Ohio Wesleyan University offers a rewarding place to work!   To discover why OWU should be your next work home, visit  our website . Learn more about our benefits at  Discover our Benefits .",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200978524879_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Director of Student Accounts and Bursar",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-15\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nOhio Wesleyan University is seeking an experienced higher education student accounts leader to serve as its Director of Student Accounts and Bursar . This position offers a unique opportunity to combine student financial services expertise, operational leadership, and student engagement to support student success and the University’s mission. The Director of Student Accounts and Bursar reports to the Controller and leads the University’s student accounts operations, including billing, cashiering, collections, account reconciliation, regulatory compliance, and student financial communications. The position also partners across campus to promote financial literacy, assist students and families in understanding their financial responsibilities, and support institutional retention efforts by helping students overcome financial barriers to enrollment and persistence. What You’ll Do As the University’s Director of Student Accounts and Bursar, you will: • Lead all aspects of student billing, payment processing, cashiering, collections, account holds, and student account operations. • Ensure the accurate assessment of tuition, fees, payments, payment plans, and refunds, including Title IV credit balances, and complete timely account reconciliations. • Develop and deliver financial literacy resources and educational programming that support informed financial decision-making. • Provide financial counseling and payment guidance to students and families while supporting student retention and persistence initiatives. • Oversee cashiering operations, collection processes, third-party and sponsor billing, and relationships with external payment and collection vendors. • Serve as the functional administrator for the University’s student accounts system (Power Campus Student Accounts). • Develop, implement, and maintain internal controls, policies, and procedures that promote financial accuracy, compliance, and operational efficiency, including payment card (PCI) compliance. • Partner with Financial Aid, Enrollment Management, Student Success, Residential Life, the Registrar, Information Services, and other campus departments to provide exceptional service to students and families. • Administer IRS Form 1098-T reporting and ensure compliance with applicable federal, state, and institutional regulations, including FERPA. • Partner with the Controller on month-end reconciliations, year-end close activities, and annual audit preparation. • Supervise and develop Student Accounts staff fostering accountability, continuous improvement, and outstanding customer service. What We’re Looking For We’re seeking an experienced higher education accounting professional who enjoys solving complex financial challenges while building strong relationships with students, families, and campus partners. Required Qualifications • Minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in student accounts, bursar operations, or student financial services within higher education. • Strong customer service, communication, and interpersonal skills. • Bachelor’s degree. • Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and Microsoft Word. • Ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities while maintaining accuracy and meeting deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Experience in one or more of the following is strongly preferred. We will support the right candidate in learning OWU-specific systems and procedures. • IRS Form 1098-T reporting and FERPA compliance. • Power Campus (Ellucian), Microsoft Dynamics GP, Flywire, Nelnet ePayment, or similar higher education enterprise systems. • Title IV credit balance and refund processing, and coordination with Financial Aid. • Cashiering, accounts receivable, and collections experience in a higher education setting. • Financial counseling or financial literacy programming. • Student retention or student success initiatives. • Advanced Microsoft Excel skills, including Pivot Tables, XLOOKUP/VLOOKUP, INDEX/MATCH, and data analysis. • Accounting process improvement, workflow automation, and operational efficiency initiatives and reporting. • Supervisory experience and staff development. Successful candidates will also demonstrate strong analytical and problem-solving abilities, sound judgment, exceptional organizational skills, and the ability to communicate financial information effectively to students, families, and colleagues from diverse backgrounds. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Why Ohio Wesleyan? Ohio Wesleyan University is a private liberal arts university in Delaware, Ohio, committed to providing a welcoming, inclusive, and student-centered environment where employees make a meaningful impact every day. As Director of Student Accounts and Bursar, you’ll play an important role in helping students successfully navigate the financial aspects of their education while ensuring the integrity and effectiveness of the University’s student financial operations. If you’re a higher education student financial services professional who works collaboratively, pursues continuous improvement, delivers exceptional customer service, and supports student success, we encourage you to apply and become part of the Ohio Wesleyan community.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200976050179_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Biological Sciences Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker –  Biological Sciences Assistant   Number of Openings: 8   Purpose/Objective of the Role: You will be assisting the Biology Laboratory Coordinators and/or Greenhouse Manager Tasks & Responsibilities:  Duties of the Biological Sciences Assistant can include:  Helping to set up and break down Biology labs, washing labware, measuring liquid and dry media, restocking lab supplies, animal care, watering plants, testing eye wash stations, repairing equipment, cleaning field lab equipment, assisting StAP and/or Museum Interns with special projects, public science outreach programs, assisting faculty members during Biol 122 laboratory sections (if qualified), following health and safety guidelines.  Animal care duties include: providing day to day support for the feeding and housing of departmental invertebrates and fish, checking/recording room temperature and humidity, cleaning fish tanks, making sure that filters, freezers, and refrigerators are operating correctly. Qualifications/Skills: Successful completion of the following courses (may be currently enrolled this semester):  Biol 120 (Introduction to Cell Biology)  Biol 122 (Organisms & Their Environment) Attention to detail Ability to work well independently and as part of a team Potential Future Career Benefit: Any field in the biological sciences   NOTE:  Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions:   Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor:  Lisa Tabak Commitment: 3-6 hours per week Term: Full Academic Year (Fall 2026 & Spring 2027), temporary, part-time position",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200976115986_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Worker - SIO Desk Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker –  SIO Desk Assistant  Number of Openings: 8 Purpose/Objective of the Role: The OWU Student Involvement Office (SIO) is seeking an enthusiastic, customer service-oriented Desk Assistants to support the daily operations of the SIO Information Desk. This role serves as the first point of contact for students, staff, and visitors. This role provides excellent customer service by assisting with campus inquiries, directing student organizations to appropriate resources, and supporting SIO programs and services. Successful candidates should demonstrate professionalism, strong communication skills, reliability, and a willingness to learn new skills, technology, and campus resources. Tasks & Responsibilities:  Attend training sessions and demonstrate proficiency in understanding of the Student Involvement Office’s services, resources, and procedures  Support and execute event management details for office events and programs  Answer phone calls, direct calls to the correct office/department, and take detailed phone messages  Manage online resources including the Student Involvement Office website, email, Engage, and HWCC digital signage  Manage and update the SIO social media accounts with information about upcoming training, events, and opportunities to get involved  Create and distribute SIO marketing to effectively promote campus events  Manage office supplies and spaces to ensure it is kept organized and tidy Qualifications/Skills: An SIO Desk Assistant should have good communication skills, must be dependable and willing to learn, and willing to provide excellent customer service.  Must be a current full-time OWU enrolled student and have federal work study. Potential Future Career Benefit: SIO Desk Assistants will gain a variety of transferable skills which include but is not limited to:  Communication skills  Customer service experience  Organizational skills  Professionalism  Experience learning new technology and office skills NOTE:  Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions:  Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor:  Dina Daltorio Commitment: 5 hours/week and additional hours for SIO programming support  Term: Full Academic Year (Fall 2026 & Spring 2027), temporary, part-time position",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200966178277_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "GMT - HVAC Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-16\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nAbout the candidate:  You are an HVAC tech with license to handle refrigerant who has a passion for building relationships and helping people. You might already have specific experience working in construction or have served in roles in the building trades. You are looking forward to working in a friendly and fast paced role on a college campus, comfortable applying your learned knowledge and skill servicing both residential and commercial facilities.  About us:  OWU Facilities Services is a dedicated group of trades and general maintenance technicians, dedicated to Ohio Wesleyan University students and the campus we collectively serve. This position has a unique opportunity to work collaboratively with many groups on campus and to be a part of a team that focuses on growing skills and developing employees.  Job Summary:  Working under general supervision, the incumbent will apply knowledge and skill to repair, install, maintain and troubleshoot heating, ventilation, air conditioning and refrigeration equipment including associated and connected equipment. Complete routine and emergency work orders. Performs preventive maintenance, as assigned. Responsibilities and duties :  Supports the efficient operation, maintenance, and testing of the University heating plant, as well as the following systems: steam distribution, pneumatic, hydronic, HVAC, refrigeration, plumbing, and energy management.  Aid in the implementation of the preventative/corrective maintenance program.  Assist in maintaining supply/inventory levels of shop requirements. Contributes to other trades and area within facilities as needed and directed by supervisor or other leadership within OWU. Helps to coordinate and supervise outside contractors/vendors who provide contractual support for the mechanical trades department functions, such as:  Chiller maintenance Boiler maintenance and inspection A/C maintenance Building sprinkler inspections Boiler water treatment PM programs Energy management Reports work rules and safety violations to the supervisor. Performs other duties as assigned. Factors contributing success:  High school diploma or GED   Vocational or technical training or degree. Universal Refrigerant License/Certification. Strong Commitment to Customer Service and a willingness to contribute across campus to support students, faculty, staff and visitors. Five (5) year’s experience in a related field such as stationary engineer, HVAC, plumbing, or refrigeration. Broad-based background and knowledge of all mechanical trades with an emphasis on HVACR and building automation systems. EPA refrigeration certification. Skill in record keeping. Knowledge and experience of: electrical control systems, motors and motor control, basic wiring methods, soldering/brazing techniques, and commercial kitchen appliances. Knowledge of National, State, and Local mechanical installation, operation, and safety codes. Skill in using MS “Word” and “Excel” software. Prior BAS experience with Delta, Ecostructure, and or Tridium is desired. The individual must also: Possess a valid Ohio driver’s license and ability to pass OWU background check. Posses a Universal license for refrigerant. Be able to lift weights common to trade. Be able to work at heights common to trade. Be on an emergency call-in rotation schedule. Must be able to be contacted 24/7 during assigned on call schedule. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States.   What We Offer: Ohio Wesleyan University offers a rewarding place to work! To discover why OWU should be your next work home, visit  our website . Learn more about our benefits at  Discover our Benefits .",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200947521006_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Bishop Scholars Tutor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-28\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nPurpose/Objective of the Role:  The Bishop Scholars Program seeks energized and committed students to tutor elementary youth in Delaware City Schools, Columbus City Schools, and Columbus Bilingual Academy North for the fall, 2026 and spring, 2027 semesters. Tutoring days include Monday,Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday with various tutoring times from approximately 8:15 a.m.– 4:00 p.m. This is a PAID position and all potential tutors must complete an in-person interview, criminal background check, and mandatory training prior to being accepted into the program. Transportation to and from our partnering schools will be provided. Tasks & Responsibilities:  Must commit to the full semester! Attend assigned day(s) of tutoring. Be on time! University transportation will leave at designated time. We will not wait for you. Wear appropriate dress attire, as outlined by OWU and our partner school guidelines. Must wear a Bishop Scholars or OWU branded shirt. Meet with assigned elementary students each scheduled day and actively interact & tutor in core competencies outlined by the partner school (Math and Reading, primarily). Complete student tutor logs each assigned day of tutoring.  Communicate attendance or program concerns to the Bishop Scholars Director at least two (2) hours prior to campus departure . Actively participate in on-campus training(s) and Lunch-and-Learns. Share the mission and work of the Bishop Scholars Program with peers in the campus community. Represent the Bishop Scholars Program on campus at Connection Conferences, symposiums, and recruitment events. Participate in and complete program surveys and reflections. Work hours must be entered into ADP on your assigned tutoring day. Qualifications: Excellent Communication Skills Time Management Skills Effective Written skills Unwavering Commitment to Attendance Strong team player with the ability to adapt to diverse team/school participants Passion for working with children and fostering a positive learning environment Spanish Speaking (preferred for one partner school, but not required) Federal Work Study Recipient (preferred, not required)   Potential Future Career Benefit: The Bishop Scholars Program provides excellent experience for students interested in the Education, Medical, or any field that requires working with the public by enhancing communication, written and interpersonal skills. Experience will include working with both children and professional staff. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Kerri Robe Commitment: 3-8 hours per week Term: temporary, part-time position  ( Fall 2026 & Spring 2027 )",
      "department": ""
    },
