    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200655037867_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "General Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2024-04-10\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nOhio Wesleyan University is a selective, private, undergraduate liberal art, residential institution founded in 1842 and located just 20 miles north of Columbus OH, is seeking candidates for two positions:  A licensed Plumber and a General Maintenance Technician with a plumbing focus.  We welcome positive, friendly and self-motivated candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of our campus community.   About you:  You are a licensed plumber or a seasoned maintenance technician who has a passion for building relationships and helping people. You might already have specific experience working in construction or have served in roles in the building trades.  You are looking forward to working in a friendly and fast paced role on a college campus, comfortable applying your earned knowledge and skill servicing both residential and commercial facilities.  About us:                         Campus Buildings and Grounds are a dedicated group of trades and general maintenance technicians, dedicated to Ohio Wesleyan University students and the campus we collectively serve.  This position has a unique opportunity to work collaboratively with many groups on campus and to be a part of a team that focuses on growing skills and developing employees.     Job Summary:  Working under general supervision, the incumbent will apply knowledge and skill at the journey level to install and repair piping, fixtures, appliances, laboratory equipment, and apparatus related to gas, air, steam, water, drainage systems, and heating and cooling systems. Complete routine and emergency work orders. Performs preventive maintenance, as assigned.   Factors contributing success:    At least five years plumbing experience in both commercial and residential construction, as well as a Plumbing Commercial Contractor’s license granted by the State of Ohio Valid driver's license and ability to meet OWU Driving Policy. a backflow tester license granted by the State of Ohio.Experience performing preventative and predictive maintenance of building systems equipment Ability to use equipment and tools effectively to perform essential job functions, demonstrate basic computer skills in order to communicate in writing as well as procure parts and interact with the computerized maintenance management system. Ability to work with and around a diverse culture  Completed application packets will include: 1)   Cover Letter with salary requirements 2)   Resume or Curriculum Vitae  WHAT WE OFFER:  Ohio Wesleyan University offers a rewarding place to work! To discover why this should be your next work home, visit our website . Learn more about our benefits at Discover our Benefits .",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200383744301_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "PT Faculty",
      "description": "Posted: 2022-04-27\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nTo move forward in the OWU new hire process, you will need to complete this system setup within ADP. This system also serves as our applicant tracking system. However, you are not considered a new applicant. Please do not be concerned by the use of the word applicant. Ultimately, the information you enter is needed to run a pre-employment background check. Once your background check is successfully completed, your new employee payroll record will also be established within this system. For any questions about this system or the OWU new hire process, please contact Human Resources at hr@owu.edu or 740/368-3388.  WHAT WE OFFER: Ohio Wesleyan University offers a rewarding place to work! To discover why this should be your next work home, visit  our website . Learn more about our benefits at  Discover our Benefits . As an equal opportunity institution, OWU has a commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and anti-racism. We do not discriminate on any basis including: race, religion, color, culture, national origin, sex and/or sexual orientation, gender, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, economic barriers, or any other legally protected factor. NOTE:  Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Candidates who accept offers of employment must be able to provide proof of their vaccination status before their employment can be process.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201869022987_2&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Research Fellow-SW",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker –  Research Fellow   Number of Openings: 1   Purpose/Objective of the Role:  A local nonprofit is rebranding and is interested in determining how effective this effort is. To gauge whether awareness of the nonprofit’s services have increased, they need a baseline measure of awareness. Working with the Community Research Fellows program at OWU, the selected students will design and conduct a market research survey of Delaware residents to glean this information from the community.   Tasks & Responsibilities: The Fellow would travel within Delaware County to conduct the survey, analyze the responses, and summarize the results for the client in a remote meeting. Qualifications/Skills:    The Fellow must be skilled in interpersonal communication and be able to convince a sufficient number of respondents to complete a brief, in-person survey. The Fellow must be an effective writer and also be able to integrate graphs, figures, and images into a report for the client. The Fellow needs to have their own vehicle and driver’s license in order to travel to multiple locations within Delaware County in order to conduct the survey.  All students with familiarity with surveys are invited to apply. Applicants are asked to send a copy of your transcript, your resume, a cover letter explaining detailing your interest, and a writing to sample to Prof. Georgic at wcgeorgic@owu.edu . Applicants are urged to apply quickly so interviews and work can begin soon. Potential Future Career Benefit:    The fellow will gain market research experience under the guidance of Prof. Georgic and the Community Research Fellows Program. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States.   Application Instructions:    Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor:  Will Georgic Commitment: 5 - hours per week Term: Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 , part-time position",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201849320162_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Videographer Intern-SW",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-25\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker - Videographer Intern (Marketing and Communications)  Number of Openings: 1   Purpose/Objective of the Role: This student will support Ohio Wesleyan University’s Marketing & Communications team by developing and producing video content that tells the OWU story. The intern will capture and edit videos for use in social media, and admission marketing, helping prospective students, alumni, and the wider community connect with the university.   Tasks & Responsibilities: Film high-quality, compelling video stories featuring OWU students, faculty, staff, and alumni. Edit short-form and long-form video content for social media, web, and promotional use. Help manage OWU’s YouTube content. Brainstorm creative content ideas in collaboration with the Marketing & Communications team. Stay attuned to video and social media trends to suggest fresh approaches. Assist with video needs at special events    Qualifications/Skills: Interest in video production, digital media, or storytelling. Experience with video editing software (Adobe Premiere Pro, Final Cut Pro, CapCut, or similar). Understanding of camera operation, lighting, and audio (training provided if needed). Strong organizational skills and ability to balance multiple projects. Creativity, curiosity, and an eye for capturing authentic, engaging moments. Good communication skills and willingness to work collaboratively. Proven ability to manage multiple short-term and long-term projects, prioritize. Turn around video projects quickly  o meet deadlines, while producing high-quality, compelling videos. Proven ability, and perform well on deadline as well as on long-term projects.   Potential Future Career Benefit: This internship is ideal for any student interested in video production, filmmaking, multimedia storytelling, social media, and/or marketing. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States   Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Kiona Dyches Commitment: 6 hours per week Term: Full Academic Year ( Fall & Spring ), temporary, part-time position",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201871210123_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nThe Opportunity  Ohio Wesleyan University’s new  Conrades School of Engineering   invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering beginning in August 2027. This is an opportunity to help build an undergraduate engineering program from the ground up, combining rigorous technical education with the breadth of the liberal arts. We seek a collaborative colleague committed to excellent teaching, student mentorship, and research involving undergraduates. Candidates from all areas of mechanical engineering are welcome.  This job is part of a cluster of positions focused on flexibility, interdisciplinarity, and inclusivity. The faculty cohort will join an educational community that values interdisciplinarity and fosters close working relationships with students through our signature program in experiential learning, the OWU Connection . Incoming faculty will be provided with mentoring, professional development, startup funds, and opportunities to connect with faculty across the Ohio 5 and GLCA consortia. For more information about the cluster, please visit www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty .   About the Conrades School of Engineering  Supported by $17 million in alumni contributions , the Conrades School of Engineering represents a sustained investment in engineering education grounded in the liberal arts. The school will welcome its first mechanical engineering majors in fall 2027, offering a  Bachelor of Science in Mechanical Engineering  and complementary minors in Engineering Science and Science and Engineering in the Public Interest. Its approach brings technical depth together with ethical reasoning, creative problem-solving, and an understanding of how engineering serves people and communities. Working closely with the Founding Dean, the successful candidate will help shape the curriculum, establish teaching laboratories, develop student research and design experiences, and prepare for ABET accreditation. The school’s location in Central Ohio offers opportunities to build relationships with employers in advanced manufacturing, technology, and related fields. We seek a colleague who brings initiative and enjoys building connections across disciplines and between classroom learning and engineering practice. Faculty support includes start-up funding, a pre-tenure sabbatical, student-faculty research opportunities through the  Summer Scholarship & Research Program  and the  OWU Connection , and mentoring and professional development through the endowed  Smith Center for Faculty Excellence . Responsibilities  Teach six courses per academic year (3/3), including first-year engineering and foundational courses such as Statics, Dynamics, and Mechanics of Materials. Upper-level courses will be added as the program grows, aligned with the candidate’s expertise and program needs.  Teach courses that contribute to the general education curriculum, including First Year Seminar.  Assist in curriculum development, revision, and evaluation with the Founding Dean, including lecture courses, laboratory courses, and engineering design experiences.  Help establish teaching laboratories, including developing experiments and identifying equipment needs.  Advise students in their academic journey and mentor their professional development.  Engage in a consistent and focused line of research that involves undergraduate students. Pursuit of external funding is encouraged.  Contribute to student recruitment, experiential learning opportunities, and relationships with external partners.  Support preparation for ABET accreditation by developing assessment tools, evaluating student learning, and documenting continuous improvement.  Provide service to the department, university, and profession.  Qualifications  Required  Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, or a closely related field, by the start of the appointment.  Experience teaching undergraduate engineering courses, including laboratory instruction.  Interest in or experience with mentoring undergraduate students, including undergraduate research.  Experience with curriculum or laboratory development, student learning assessment, or ABET accreditation.  Preferred  Engineering experience in industry.  Bachelor’s degree in mechanical engineering from an ABET-accredited program. Application Instructions  Applicants should submit the following:  Cover letter : Describe your qualifications, interest in the position, and preparation to contribute to the development of a new undergraduate mechanical engineering program within a liberal arts context.  Current curriculum vitae : Include your teaching, research, professional, and service activities.  Teaching and Student Engagement Statement (2-page limit) : Please provide a statement that articulates your teaching philosophy. In your response, address your ability to teach a broad range of courses and to employ pedagogical approaches that support students with varied perspectives and experiences. Describe how you connect students with opportunities, resources, and networks that expand their access to the field of mechanical engineering. Include examples of outreach, advising, or program activities that have supported students whose pathways into mechanical engineering may not follow a traditional trajectory. Address classroom and laboratory instruction.  Research statement (2-page limit) : Outline the research program you would develop at OWU, including its central aims, how it will thrive at Ohio Wesleyan, opportunities for meaningful undergraduate participation, and the facilities and resources needed to establish it.  Please submit all materials, preferably in pdf format, via www.owu.edu/joinOWUfaculty , where you will find additional information about working at OWU. To be considered for the initial round of review, you must submit your cover letter, CV, teaching and student engagement statement, research statement, and contacts for three professional references. Official transcripts, reference letters, and additional materials may be requested at a later time and can be sent directly to facultyjobs@owu.edu . Questions about the position may be directed to Paul Slaboch, Founding Dean of the Conrades School of Engineering and Search Chair, at peslaboch@owu.edu . For questions, including difficulty with uploading materials, contact facultyjobs@owu.edu and include the search number in the subject line. Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled.   About Ohio Wesleyan University  Located in the Columbus, Ohio metropolitan area, Ohio Wesleyan is a selective residential liberal arts college enrolling approximately 1,600+ students from across the nation and around the world. The college’s signature program, the OWU Connection, empowers students to complete research, community service, careers, and study abroad, teaching students to apply their knowledge in real-world settings. Ohio Wesleyan is featured in the book Colleges That Change Lives and was recently listed as the No. 1 liberal arts college in Ohio for social mobility by U.S. News and World Report. OWU is located in Delaware, OH, a lively college town just 30 minutes from Columbus, the 14th most populous city in the United States and part of the fastest growing, most economically vibrant areas of the Midwest. Columbus, known increasingly as the “Silicon Midwest,” was named by LinkedIn as one of the top 10 U.S. cities in which to launch your career. To achieve our mission, we continually strive to foster a campus community where every individual is respected, supported, and able to flourish. We affirm the worth of all persons and welcome people of all backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. Ohio Wesleyan University is an equal opportunity institution and seeks applications from individuals who will contribute to, and help strengthen, our commitment to academic excellence, mutual respect, and the shared pursuit of knowledge.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201870788520_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Worker-History",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker – History Spring 2027  Number of Openings: 1 Purpose/Objective of the Role:  To assist Academic Assistant and Faculty with operations of the department and preparation for classes. Tasks & Responsibilities : Check Mail/duplicating Update bulletin board Create and post flyers for upcoming events, attend events, assist with needs for lectures Scan documents and save to appropriate drive Qualifications:  Canva experience for making flyers, invitations, and other documents General office skills Potential Future Career Benefit: To gain experience in general office skills, become familiar with the working of an academic office, and develop relationships and networking skills. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States.   Application Instructions :  Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor:  Jennifer Seely Commitment: 8-10 hours per week Term:  Spring 2027 temporary, part-time position",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201872523641_2&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Floor Associate",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\n\nLocation: Delaware\n\nStudent Worker –  Floor Associate   Number of Openings: 1   Purpose/Objective of the Role:     Welcome all to The 1842. Taking care of The 1842 by removing trash, cleaning up spills, setting up games/activities, and reporting problems that may arise.   Tasks & Responsibilities :   Provide welcoming atmosphere Empty trash and recycling cans when they become full Clean up spills of beverage and food Dispose of trash and wipe down tables in between uses Provide tv channel changes when requested Help in completing opening and closing tasks Once an hour bathroom and patio checks for tidiness Helping to set up, run, and tear down special events Report of equipment that is broken or not functioning as intended Report any actions or incidents that jeopardize student safety, damage property, or are unlawful that occur on the grounds of the facility Other duties as assigned     Qualifications/Skills:   Willingness to work with others Good communication skills Available to work nights and weekends   Potential Future Career Benefit: Hospitality experience Working in group settings   NOTE:  Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States.   Application Instructions :   Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor:  Anna Pellegrin Commitment: 5-20 hours per week Rate of pay is $11.00 an hour Term: Fall & Spring – (26/27) (temporary, part-time position)",
